DESCRIPTION:Born in a bomb shelter beneath the Kremlin and rumoured to be V
 ladimir Putin's nephew\, Sergei Putinski defies convention and thrives on t
 he absurd. With an unwavering love for 80s sitcoms and the firm belief that
  technology peaked in 1992\, he navigates the modern world behind the wheel
  of a beat-up Maserati\, barking into a giant white cell phone. With hundre
 ds of millions of views online and crowds that match his energy beat for be
 at\, Sergei delivers a live experience that blends sharp stand-up\, unhinge
 d crowdwork\, and a torrent of surreal hot-takes. It's part fever dream\, p
 art social satire\, and entirely unforgettable.\n\nThere is a two-item per 
 person minimum in the Showroom\, which can be fulfilled with any food or dr
 ink items from the menu.\n\nPLEASE NOTE: Food and drinks purchased in the b
 ar and lounge do not count towards the two-item minimum.\n\nManagement rese
 rves the right to prevent customers from entering the facility who they dee
 m disruptive or dangerous to other patrons.\nMore info: https://comedyatlas
